     "vocals": "Smooth, airy tenor with warm tone and flexible falsetto; relaxed, rhythmic phrasing, melismatic ornamentation and an intimate delivery suited to Afropop and R&B-inflected productions.",
     "aliases": [
      "Wizkid",
      "Wiz",
      "Lil Prinz",
      "Starboy"
     ],
     "members": [],
     "is_group": false,
     "biography": "Born Ayodeji Ibrahim Balogun in Surulere, Lagos, Wizkid began singing in church at age 11 under the name \"Lil Prinz.\" He rebranded around 2006 and worked his way through the Nigerian music scene, signing early with local labels before achieving mainstream breakthrough in 2010 with singles like \"Holla At Your Boy,\" \"Tease Me\" and \"Don't Dull.\" His debut album Superstar (2011) cemented his status in Nigeria; he later founded Starboy Entertainment and expanded internationally with collaborations and releases that pushed Afrobeats onto global charts.",
     "known_for": "Smooth melodic vocals, trendsetting Afrobeats hits, international collaborations, and helping globalize Nigerian pop music.",
     "start_year": 2006,
     "voice_type": [
      "Tenor"
     ],
     "description": "Wizkid (Ayodeji Ibrahim Balogun), also known as Starboy, is a Nigerian singer-songwriter and one of the leading figures of contemporary Afrobeats. Rising from singing in church as a child to international stardom, he blends Afropop, R&B and dancehall influences, has multiple charting singles and albums, and is noted for major collaborations with global artists that helped bring Nigerian music to mainstream global audiences.",
